SED(1)                      User Commands                    SED(1)

NAME
    sed - stream editor

SYNOPSIS
    sed [-Ealnru] command [file...]
    sed [-Ealnru] [-e command] [-f command_file] [-i extension] [file...]

DESCRIPTION
    sed reads each input line, applies the editing commands and writes the
    result to standard output. Without files it reads standard input.

OPTIONS
    -E            use extended regular expressions
    -a            open w files when first written to
    -e command    add command to the script; may be repeated
    -f file       add the commands in file to the script; may be repeated
    -i extension  edit files in place; a copy is kept with the extension
                  appended, or none when the extension is empty
    -l            line buffer the output
    -n            print only lines selected with p
    -r            same as -E
    -u            unbuffer the output

COMMANDS
    An address is a line number, $, or /regex/; two addresses separated by
    a comma select a range. ! after the address negates it.

    s/re/rep/flags  substitute; flags g, p, N (the Nth match), I, w file
    y/from/to/      transliterate
    p  P            print the pattern space; print its first line
    d  D            delete the pattern space; delete its first line
    n  N            next line; append the next line
    g  G  h  H  x   copy or append between the pattern and hold spaces
    a\ i\ c\        append, insert or change text; the text follows on the
                    next line
    r file  w file  read a file after the line; write the line to a file
    b  t  T label   branch; branch if a substitution was made; if none was
    :label          define a label; it extends to the end of the line
    =  l  q         print the line number; print unambiguously; quit
    { commands }    group commands

EXAMPLES
    sed -n '2,4p' file
    sed -e 's/x/y/' -e 't done' -e 's/$/!/' -e ':done' file
    sed -i '' 's/old/new/g' file

SEE ALSO
    awk(1), grep(1)
